Old review:
- If you liked Titan Quest, you'll love this one! It's an indie title made by 8 people who previously worked on Titan Quest, and it shows. And even on Early Access the game already has all most of the content made, and it's very, very playable at this state.
New:
- Amazing to see the game finished, it's just an amazing polished experience.
It's just fun to create a characther, level up, choose your skills (you can make really unique classes, and the way the skill system works, makes for a lot of room for choices). Experimenting with different loot is rewarding and the killing is always fun and it has a good amount of content to be enjoyed.
The story is good and combines well with the feeling of the world (It's a Grim world out there).
The developers keep updating the game with content and polishing the expirence even more. The game has got tons of support.
Pros:
+ Great art style and dark tone;
+ Immersive soundtrack;
+ Great loot (balanced);
+ The "skill tree" is fun to explore for every mastery;
+ There's a lot of room to create a unique character seeing that you can combine two different masteries to the same character, but cannot max out the skills on both (you'll have to make choices);
+ Secrets (they are very well hidden and feel rewarding to find);
+ Devotion skill tree incentivises exploring to find the points to spend on it (devotion skill tree is a separated skill tree that let's you spend points aquired from Shrines scattered throughout the world and gives you extra level of character development).
Cons:
- Animations are a bit stiff (but is not that bad);
- The late game right now consists of replaying the campaign with an increased difficulty and some rogue dungeons (although is fun).

